MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

> In which case I'm declaring parameters (in B) that don't get used in the model. Is this going to be a problem?

It won’t technically lead to sampling problems provided that the unused parameters have
well-posed priors, in which case you reduce to sampling from those priors.

> (Note I've not implemented one of these models in Stan yet, but I am considering a large project and I'm trying to think through the potential issues).

The reason why this seems awkward is because it is!  When you want to impose causal
constraints like this you need to impose generative structure in your model, not hack
stochastic structure.  That would mean building an explicit model for the Australian
economy as a function of the American economy.  Of course this can be anathema
to economists so you might be in between awkward hacks and fighting conventions...

