Don’t do real<lower=0.0001> sigma.  It should be real<lower=0>.  Also I recommend not using the inverse gamma prior distribution on sigma.  It’s non-intuitive, i.e. if you use it you could well be including prior information you don’t really want to include.  Also I don’t know how many cutpoints you have but it seems to me kinda weird to give them a common normal(3,1) prior.

