That would be great.  The whole “Bayesian model averaging” thing has been a useless time sink for decades.

> On Feb 7, 2016, at 11:14 PM, Michael Betancourt <betan...@gmail.com> wrote:
>

> We need to stop having these discussions over the weekend!  Mike West has been
> doing some brilliant work that generalizes all of this as a hierarchical model over
> models.  It goes beyond the typical machine learning approaches and Bayesian
> model comparison approaches into one coherent framework where you can choose
> the mixture weights based on your own self-consistent criterion.
>
