Hi list,

so I was wondering wether it was possible in STAN to get intermediate leapfrog steps from the HMC/NUTS sampler, for example to do something like Nishimura & Dunson <http://arxiv.org/abs/1511.06925>. Also, is it still the case that STAN estimates the diagonal of the target covariance from burn-in as in the NUTS paper? Or is it approximating the full rank matrix now? Other notable differences from the NUTS paper?

Thanks
Ingmar

