Hi Bob,

I sent a pull request under Stan/stan-dev. The name of the branch is charlesm93:CompartmentModelGrammar.

Checking ast.hpp, I believe I did include the new structure in the expression variant type:

    struct expression {
      typedef boost::variant<boost::recursive_wrapper<nil>,
                             boost::recursive_wrapper<int_literal>,
                             boost::recursive_wrapper<double_literal>,
                             boost::recursive_wrapper<array_literal>,
                             boost::recursive_wrapper<variable>,
                             boost::recursive_wrapper<integrate_ode>,
                             boost::recursive_wrapper<integrate_ode_cvode>,
                             boost::recursive_wrapper<GeneralCptModel_CVODE>,
                             boost::recursive_wrapper<fun>,
                             boost::recursive_wrapper<index_op>,
                             boost::recursive_wrapper<index_op_sliced>,
                             boost::recursive_wrapper<binary_op>,
                             boost::recursive_wrapper<unary_op> >
      expression_t;

I deleted CmdStan and reinstalled it from scratch. This actually made a difference, but I do not have a solid theory as to why. Still, the building of CmdStan was not complete, and the compiler returned the following two error messages:

> stan/lib/stan_math/lib/boost_1.58.0/boost/fusion/container/vector/convert.hpp:25:30: error: implicit
>
>      instantiation of undefined template 'boost::fusion::detail::barrier::as_vector<13>'
>
>            typedef typename gen::
>
>                              ^
>
>
> stan/lib/stan_math/lib/boost_1.58.0/boost/fusion/container/vector/convert.hpp:26:26: error: 'apply'
>
>      following the 'template' keyword does not refer to a template
>
>                template apply<typename result_of::begin<Sequence>::type>::type
>
>
>
Looking at the endless lines detailing the first error message on terminal, I'm guessing the line that causes the error is in term_grammar_def.hpp, line 1189:
>
>
>         GeneralCptModel_CVODE_r
>         %= (lit("GeneralCptModel_CVODE") >> no_skip[!char_("a-zA-Z0-9_")])
>         > lit('(')
>         > identifier_r        // system function name (function only)
>         > lit(',')
>         > expression_g(_r1)		// pMatrix
>         > lit(',')
