Hi, yes, this is a great example and worth thinking about further.  Yet another approach that has been suggested is to weight each model proportional to exp(-LOO).  In the asymptotic limit, this will pick the single best-fit model.  To the extent that different models fit well to different data, a mixture could makes sense.  This is somethign worth discussing.
A

