I have some rough understanding of how the warmup procedure works, but it's not entirely clear to me whether the fact that it is 'slow' (roughly 10x slower than sampling, per iteration) is something that can be substantially improved by adjusting parameters (so far I have just set the initial step size to roughly that used by NUTS during sampling), or whether this slowness is inherent to the problems of a) sampling towards high mass regions, and b) estimating the metric. Is there anything useful one can take from one fit procedure to the next, when fitting similar models with a similar parameter space, to different data?

