Thanks for the update.

g++ 4.2's compile time is very slow relative to a more recent version of g++ (4.6 or 4.8) and clang++, so I'll definitely suggest compiling with clang++ if you can.

90+ mins doesn't seem normal. Is there a difference in time with clang++?

Daniel

On Mon, Feb 15, 2016 at 2:02 PM, Jökull Snæbjarnarson <jok...@gmail.com> wrote:
> Hi again Daniel.
> The code is 10 k lines.
> The stanc compiler correctly translates from Stan to C++.
