I saw on the web an idea <http://jofrhwld.github.io/blog/2014/07/29/nonlinear_stan.html> for modeling non-linear relationships that I'm playing around with in Stan but am finding it difficult to implement.  Probably, a huge part of this difficulty is knowing what to do once I've diagnosed a sampling problem.  The issue has been a large number of divergent transitions happening after warmup is complete.  I've tried adding stronger priors, increasing adapt_delta (as suggested in the information message).  Despite setting adapt_delta to several higher values (and having to increase max_treedepth) I still get divergent transitions.  Obviously, there's either a) something wrong with my code, or b) this is just a really difficult posterior to sample from.  Does anyone have any thoughts—any help would be greatly appreciated?  Code and sessionInfo() below.

sessionInfo:

R version 3.2.3 (2015-12-10)
Platform: x86_64-apple-darwin13.4.0 (64-bit)
Running under: OS X 10.10.5 (Yosemite)

locale:
