Hi Guido,

Can you first clean everything now that you've changed compilers:
make clean-all

Then run it again and please provide the full output. I'm not sure where it's failing when I'm only seeing bits of the linking, bits of compiler warnings (that don't happen on linking, so I don't know if there's something happening out of order), and it would be good to see what you are using to call the compiled Stan program.

If the Stan program with the data works on Windows and Mac, we may be dealing with an incompatibility with Intel's c++ compiler, which is known to not be fully compatible with the c++ spec. We don't have access to the compiler, so the best we can do is help is have you describe everything and hopefully we spot the problem.

Daniel

